1
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:10,920
Daddy, kiss Mommy on the cheek too.

2
00:03:11,440 --> 00:03:14,080
I don't care who that woman is.

3
00:03:14,160 --> 00:03:16,760
But you are not allowed to hurt my son.

4
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:20,440
I think Papang is old enough. Wouldn't it
be better if we told him the truth?

5
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:23,520
But remember,
you absolutely cannot tell Papang

6
00:03:23,600 --> 00:03:25,120
why you're staying here.

7
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:27,920
The fact that everyone wrongly
believes we slept together

8
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,760
is the most embarrassing thing
that has ever happened to me.

9
00:03:31,440 --> 00:03:34,840
Chayanee loves me very much.
She'll definitely get the money for us.

10
00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:37,960
I'm giving the money to Raiwin
for his election campaign.

11
00:03:38,040 --> 00:03:39,120
PREVIOUSLY

12
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:43,920
Uncle, here's a ten-million-baht check.

13
00:03:55,760 --> 00:03:58,600
Chayanee, you're the sweetest.

14
00:03:58,680 --> 00:04:01,280
I always keep my word.

15
00:04:02,040 --> 00:04:05,360
If I say I'll get something done,
I get it done.

16
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:10,000
But can you promise me two things?

17
00:04:10,920 --> 00:04:14,200
Of course. Whatever you want me to do,

18
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:16,800
I'll do everything I can to help.

19
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:20,200
You have to make sure
Raiwin wins the election.

20
00:04:20,279 --> 00:04:22,720
And if the Subdistrict Office
has any projects,

21
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:25,280
they must prioritize
Grandpa's company's interests.

22
00:04:26,200 --> 00:04:30,000
You really are the beloved granddaughter
of a major businessman.

23
00:04:30,800 --> 00:04:32,600
Yes, an investment
has to generate a return.

24
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:36,280
You can trust me. I'll do everything I can

25
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:39,000
to make sure Raiwin wins the election,

26
00:04:39,080 --> 00:04:43,160
and then we'll build him up
into a national-level politician.

27
00:04:45,440 --> 00:04:48,840
I'll do my best to become Chief
and make you my wife.

28
00:04:48,920 --> 00:04:50,760
By the way,

29
00:04:50,840 --> 00:04:53,880
what's the second thing you want me to do?

30
00:04:56,880 --> 00:05:00,800
You have to make sure Raiwin
is above Ramil in every way.

31
00:05:01,320 --> 00:05:03,520
Status, reputation.

32
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:06,760
And I have to be above Hathaya.

33
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:10,200
I'll do everything I can.

34
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:15,160
My son and my future daughter-in-law

35
00:05:16,240 --> 00:05:18,320
have to be better than those parasites.

36
00:05:23,240 --> 00:05:26,440
I'll excuse myself.

37
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:28,240
Raiwin, take good care of her.

38
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:43,120
Papang.

39
00:05:45,400 --> 00:05:47,480
Papang, are you done washing your face?

40
00:05:49,920 --> 00:05:51,200
Papang.

41
00:05:56,240 --> 00:05:57,280
Papang.

42
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:03,600
Where are you?

43
00:06:14,760 --> 00:06:15,800
Papang.

44
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:18,160
Papang?

45
00:06:19,760 --> 00:06:20,880
Papang.

46
00:06:22,520 --> 00:06:26,760
I'm gone. I'm going home.

47
00:06:31,920 --> 00:06:33,000
Papang.

48
00:06:34,200 --> 00:06:35,240
Papang!

49
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:38,680
Hey! Look, I bought a lot of food.

50
00:06:38,760 --> 00:06:41,160
Ramil! Papang is gone.

51
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:44,200
-What? Where did he go?
-He ran away to go home.

52
00:06:46,520 --> 00:06:49,480
He couldn't have gotten far.
Let's search inside the development first.

53
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:50,480
Okay.

54
00:06:56,640 --> 00:06:58,520
Papang, Ramil's son, ran away from home.

55
00:06:58,600 --> 00:07:00,880
Everyone over there
is searching everywhere for him.

56
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:03,560
Then…

57
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:06,560
Call everyone in the house.
Have them help search for Papang.

58
00:07:06,640 --> 00:07:07,480
Yes.

59
00:07:09,960 --> 00:07:11,200
What happened, Auntie?

60
00:07:11,280 --> 00:07:13,320
Papang ran away from home.

61
00:07:14,640 --> 00:07:17,600
Papang? Whose child is Papang?

62
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:20,520
-Papang is the child of--
-Ramil and Nuchwara.

63
00:07:21,520 --> 00:07:22,880
Ramil's child?

64
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:26,280
I had no idea Ramil kept the baby.

65
00:07:26,360 --> 00:07:28,760
I thought he made
Nuchwara get an abortion.

66
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:32,880
Now I'm curious whether the child
looks more like his father or his mother.

67
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:36,480
Don't worry about it. Weren't you hungry?

68
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:38,400
Let's go get something to eat.

69
00:07:44,520 --> 00:07:47,240
Excuse me. Have you seen
this child come through here?

70
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:49,840
No, I haven't. I haven't seen him.

71
00:07:49,920 --> 00:07:51,640
Thank you very much.

72
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:54,360
Excuse me. Have you seen
this child around here?

73
00:07:54,440 --> 00:07:55,400
No, I haven't.

74
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:56,720
You haven't?

75
00:07:56,800 --> 00:07:57,640
Thank you very much.

76
00:07:57,720 --> 00:07:59,800
Excuse me. Have you seen this child?

77
00:08:00,360 --> 00:08:01,280
No.

78
00:08:01,360 --> 00:08:03,280
Thank you.

79
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:05,120
Any luck?

80
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:07,720
Nothing. I asked around,
and no one has seen him.

81
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:10,600
I searched everywhere too. Nothing.

82
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:12,640
What if Papang
made it out to the main road?

83
00:08:14,600 --> 00:08:16,480
Two-eight slash six-one, hurry!

84
00:08:16,560 --> 00:08:17,560
Excuse me.

85
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:20,480
-What happened?
-A child was hit by a car.

86
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:21,560
What?

87
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:22,720
Let's go.

88
00:08:26,760 --> 00:08:28,200
AUTHORIZED EMERGENCY VEHICLE

89
00:08:28,280 --> 00:08:30,040
Sir! How is my son?

90
00:08:31,520 --> 00:08:33,559
It isn't a boy. The child is a girl.

91
00:08:33,640 --> 00:08:35,600
Her father got into
the ambulance with her.

92
00:08:35,679 --> 00:08:38,240
-It isn't a boy?
-No.

93
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:44,640
Then where is Papang?

94
00:08:44,720 --> 00:08:48,440
What if he's hiding in the house?
Maybe he was just trying to scare me!

95
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:50,600
Papang!

96
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:13,280
Serves that

97
00:09:13,360 --> 00:09:15,200
witch auntie right.

98
00:09:15,280 --> 00:09:18,960
Daddy will yell at her
and kick her out of the house.

99
00:09:20,640 --> 00:09:23,120
I'm going to find Daddy.

100
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:26,160
-Still nothing?
-No.

101
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:29,400
Then have everyone split up
and search again.

102
00:09:29,480 --> 00:09:30,440
Yes.

103
00:09:34,960 --> 00:09:37,400
-Have you found him yet?
-Not yet.

104
00:09:38,840 --> 00:09:40,240
Don't worry about it.

105
00:09:40,320 --> 00:09:43,160
Let his parents look for him.

106
00:09:43,240 --> 00:09:46,680
It's sad, really.
What kind of parents are they

107
00:09:46,760 --> 00:09:48,640
if their kid doesn't
even want to stay with them?

108
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:51,440
Come on. I'm hungry.

109
00:09:58,600 --> 00:09:59,680
Bye.

110
00:10:02,760 --> 00:10:05,320
Come to think of it,

111
00:10:05,400 --> 00:10:08,240
I am curious whether the boy looks
more like his father or his mother.

112
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:12,000
Forget about him.
What do you want to eat today? My treat.

113
00:10:12,760 --> 00:10:14,880
-Let's go.
-Okay.

114
00:10:21,680 --> 00:10:22,520
Watch out!

115
00:10:27,680 --> 00:10:28,520
You crazy kid!

116
00:10:28,600 --> 00:10:30,160
You ran right in front of the car!

117
00:10:30,240 --> 00:10:33,320
If my boyfriend hadn't braked in time,
the car would've hit you and killed you!

118
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:36,280
And if the car had hit and killed you,

119
00:10:36,360 --> 00:10:39,120
he would've been in trouble.
Didn't your parents teach you anything?!

120
00:10:40,800 --> 00:10:43,200
Papang.

121
00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:44,600
Let's go.

122
00:10:45,400 --> 00:10:47,720
If no one ever taught this child better,

123
00:10:47,800 --> 00:10:49,440
I guess

124
00:10:50,280 --> 00:10:54,680
no one ever taught you either.
No wonder you're so narrow-minded.

125
00:10:55,360 --> 00:10:57,400
Instead of pitying him
and warning him calmly,

126
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:59,440
all you can do is yell
and worry about yourself!

127
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:08,920
Raiwin, your brother is standing here
insulting me. Do something!

128
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:13,200
Chayanee.

129
00:11:15,120 --> 00:11:16,320
Calm down.

130
00:11:16,400 --> 00:11:17,960
Let's go.

131
00:11:19,160 --> 00:11:20,000
Come on.

132
00:11:31,440 --> 00:11:32,320
Ramil.

133
00:11:33,320 --> 00:11:36,720
Take the kid home.
Don't let him run around outside.

134
00:11:51,360 --> 00:11:54,360
It's okay, Papang. Don't be scared.

135
00:11:54,920 --> 00:11:55,840
Papang.

136
00:11:55,920 --> 00:11:59,960
Papang. Never do this again.

137
00:12:00,560 --> 00:12:03,960
Don't lie to Aunt Hathaya again,
and don't run out into the road like that.

138
00:12:04,040 --> 00:12:07,800
I'm sorry. But the witch auntie
is always mean to me.

139
00:12:07,880 --> 00:12:10,320
She doesn't love me.

140
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:12,560
I don't want to stay with her.

141
00:12:12,640 --> 00:12:16,080
I teach you because I care about you.

142
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:18,280
You shouldn't do something like this.

143
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:22,320
You lied and caused all this trouble.

144
00:12:23,080 --> 00:12:26,080
Look how worried everyone became
because of what you did.

145
00:12:26,160 --> 00:12:27,920
Daddy was extremely worried about you too.

146
00:12:28,920 --> 00:12:32,880
If you keep crying wolf like this,
no one will believe you anymore.

147
00:12:35,280 --> 00:12:38,240
That's enough. I'll teach Papang myself.

148
00:12:41,240 --> 00:12:42,320
Daddy is here now.

149
00:12:42,400 --> 00:12:46,240
From now on, I won't let anyone
hurt you again, okay?

150
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:50,040
Stop crying. You're a boy.
You have to be strong. Understand?

151
00:13:03,760 --> 00:13:05,280
Is Papang asleep?

152
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:11,080
I think

153
00:13:12,200 --> 00:13:15,000
you need to be stricter with him.

154
00:13:15,080 --> 00:13:18,280
Otherwise, he'll keep acting spoiled
and demanding things from you.

155
00:13:19,720 --> 00:13:20,560
I can't do that.

156
00:13:23,360 --> 00:13:25,280
I don't want to make him sad.

157
00:13:27,240 --> 00:13:30,920
If you give in to everything,
he'll keep demanding whatever he wants.

158
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:33,760
And he'll keep doing it.

159
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:35,960
He'll grow up spoiled.

160
00:13:36,760 --> 00:13:39,120
Don't be the parent
who harms your child by spoiling him.

161
00:13:40,040 --> 00:13:43,440
Your job is to teach him
how to live properly.

162
00:13:43,520 --> 00:13:44,360
Enough.

163
00:13:45,120 --> 00:13:46,680
Whatever Papang wants,

164
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:49,040
I'm not going to deny him.

165
00:13:50,840 --> 00:13:53,640
Why? I don't understand.

166
00:13:53,720 --> 00:13:55,840
If something had happened to Papang today,

167
00:13:56,720 --> 00:13:58,320
I would've felt incredibly guilty.

168
00:13:59,240 --> 00:14:00,680
Guilty for leaving him.

169
00:14:01,880 --> 00:14:05,080
And I thought you would
take better care of him,

170
00:14:05,160 --> 00:14:06,920
but you upset him too.

171
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:09,000
From now on,

172
00:14:10,560 --> 00:14:12,640
I won't make Papang unhappy again

173
00:14:13,680 --> 00:14:15,400
because I understand him.

174
00:14:19,640 --> 00:14:23,400
If that's how you feel,
I can't argue with you.

175
00:14:24,760 --> 00:14:26,320
Papang is your son.

176
00:14:58,640 --> 00:15:01,320
You never come anywhere near this house.

177
00:15:02,800 --> 00:15:04,520
What brings you here?

178
00:15:05,400 --> 00:15:06,520
Is Papang asleep?

179
00:15:09,160 --> 00:15:12,240
What got into you?
Since when do you care about the kid?

180
00:15:12,320 --> 00:15:15,160
I want you to take
Papang back to his mother.

181
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:17,680
I don't want him staying here.

182
00:15:18,520 --> 00:15:21,400
Are you afraid he'll get into
another accident like today?

183
00:15:22,840 --> 00:15:24,640
Or are you afraid the truth will come out?

184
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:28,040
Dad, Nuchwara is pregnant.

185
00:15:29,280 --> 00:15:32,240
I told you!

186
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:36,480
You can have fun,
but you have to protect yourself!

187
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:41,040
I tried, Dad, but Nuchwara
wouldn't take birth control pills.

188
00:15:41,640 --> 00:15:42,640
You idiot!

189
00:15:43,560 --> 00:15:46,200
Dad, what am I supposed to do?

190
00:15:47,680 --> 00:15:51,080
-Get rid of the baby.
-Nuchwara refuses to have an abortion.

191
00:15:51,640 --> 00:15:53,920
She threatened that if I force her,

192
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:56,400
she'll report it to the university
and expose me.

193
00:15:56,480 --> 00:15:58,600
She was trying to trap you.

194
00:15:58,680 --> 00:16:00,960
She thought she could
come live comfortably here.

195
00:16:01,040 --> 00:16:03,840
I sent you to school
so you could graduate.

196
00:16:03,920 --> 00:16:06,280
You cannot have a scandal on your record.

197
00:16:06,360 --> 00:16:09,280
And most importantly,
you cannot become a father right now!

198
00:16:09,360 --> 00:16:10,640
Then what are you going to do?

199
00:16:14,800 --> 00:16:15,840
Ramil.

200
00:16:17,280 --> 00:16:20,640
You'll claim the baby
as yours instead of Raiwin.

201
00:16:23,360 --> 00:16:25,560
That's his problem.
It has nothing to do with me!

202
00:16:25,640 --> 00:16:28,040
You live in my house.

203
00:16:28,120 --> 00:16:31,800
You. Tell your son to agree.

204
00:16:31,880 --> 00:16:34,560
If he refuses, both of you,
get out of this house.

205
00:16:41,640 --> 00:16:44,600
Mom! How many times has this happened?

206
00:16:45,240 --> 00:16:48,280
His son causes trouble, and I'm always
the one who has to cover for him!

207
00:16:48,960 --> 00:16:50,720
And you keep giving in to them.

208
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:53,560
Ramil, I'm begging you.

209
00:16:54,240 --> 00:16:56,080
Mr. Saksit has done so much for us.

210
00:16:56,840 --> 00:16:58,280
You were able to attend a good school

211
00:16:58,360 --> 00:17:01,360
and have a good home and food
because he helped us.

212
00:17:01,440 --> 00:17:04,160
Mom! You expect me to claim a child

213
00:17:04,240 --> 00:17:06,119
who isn't even my own?

214
00:17:06,800 --> 00:17:09,400
What about my life? What about my future?!

215
00:17:13,359 --> 00:17:14,280
Ramil.

216
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:20,079
Nuchwara just called and threatened
to kill herself. If she does,

217
00:17:20,160 --> 00:17:24,040
this will all come back to me.
Ramil, please help me. Please.

218
00:17:25,599 --> 00:17:26,640
Please.

219
00:17:27,160 --> 00:17:29,160
Please, Ramil. Help me.

220
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:32,480
Claim the baby as yours.

221
00:17:32,560 --> 00:17:35,680
I'll give Nuchwara money
and have her take care of herself.

222
00:17:35,760 --> 00:17:38,240
You won't have to do anything.

223
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:42,000
Please help me.
I'll never forget what you did for me.

224
00:17:43,520 --> 00:17:46,800
I agreed to be Papang's father
because I felt sorry for Nuchwara.

225
00:17:48,840 --> 00:17:50,640
I let everyone misunderstand

226
00:17:50,720 --> 00:17:52,840
and think I was the bad guy.

227
00:17:53,760 --> 00:17:57,160
But what about you? Have you ever
taken responsibility for what you did?

228
00:17:57,760 --> 00:18:00,760
And now you're asking me
to send Papang far away.

229
00:18:00,840 --> 00:18:02,280
You're that scared, aren't you?

230
00:18:03,040 --> 00:18:06,680
Scared Chayanee will find out
that Papang is your son.

231
00:18:06,760 --> 00:18:10,560
Yes. I'm afraid Chayanee will find out.

232
00:18:11,480 --> 00:18:15,480
Candidate registration is coming up.
I don't want anyone digging into my past.

233
00:18:15,560 --> 00:18:16,920
No matter what happens,

234
00:18:18,480 --> 00:18:20,360
I will never abandon Papang.

235
00:18:21,240 --> 00:18:24,640
If you want him to stay here,
I won't stop you.

236
00:18:26,040 --> 00:18:27,240
But I'm asking you

237
00:18:27,880 --> 00:18:29,880
to keep him away from the main house.

238
00:18:32,440 --> 00:18:34,840
And keep the promise you made me.

239
00:18:36,280 --> 00:18:39,680
Papang is your son. Not mine.

240
00:18:43,280 --> 00:18:45,840
Tell me the truth.
Have you ever loved your own child?

241
00:19:02,040 --> 00:19:03,280
Chamoi.

242
00:19:04,600 --> 00:19:07,640
-Has Father not come downstairs yet?
-He already did.

243
00:19:08,360 --> 00:19:11,600
I asked Chamoi, my servant.
Mind your own business.

244
00:19:11,680 --> 00:19:13,560
Sorry,

245
00:19:13,640 --> 00:19:17,720
but your servant is in the kitchen
scrolling through videos, doing zero work.

246
00:19:17,800 --> 00:19:20,720
That woman never learns.

247
00:19:22,960 --> 00:19:25,320
If Grandpa already came down, where is he?

248
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:28,960
He already ate breakfast
and took his medicine.

249
00:19:29,040 --> 00:19:30,880
He left for the development early.

250
00:19:32,320 --> 00:19:35,280
What? Why did Father leave so early today?

251
00:19:48,080 --> 00:19:49,920
Anything you would like me to do, sir?

252
00:19:53,720 --> 00:19:57,640
What? Okay. I'll be there right away.

253
00:20:00,480 --> 00:20:02,800
Someone from your office called?
What happened?

254
00:20:02,880 --> 00:20:06,200
Grandpa came to ask to inspect
the accounting documents.

255
00:20:06,720 --> 00:20:08,440
We need to get there right away. Come on.

256
00:20:08,520 --> 00:20:10,720
Why are you panicking?

257
00:20:11,880 --> 00:20:14,560
Or did you embezzle Grandpa's money?

258
00:20:15,960 --> 00:20:18,720
Oh, please. I only adjusted
the figures a little.

259
00:20:19,400 --> 00:20:21,320
If I didn't,

260
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:24,680
where would you get all the money
you spend shopping so freely?

261
00:20:24,760 --> 00:20:26,000
Stop asking questions.

262
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:34,960
Please, let him finally catch them.

263
00:20:35,040 --> 00:20:37,880
I feel so sorry for him.

264
00:20:39,560 --> 00:20:42,040
These are the updated reservations.
Report to Mr. Pichai.

265
00:20:42,120 --> 00:20:43,160
-Of course.
-Thank you.

266
00:20:44,240 --> 00:20:45,160
Wait.

267
00:20:45,760 --> 00:20:48,040
Where are you taking those documents?

268
00:20:48,680 --> 00:20:50,320
Mr. Pichai asked to inspect them.

269
00:20:50,400 --> 00:20:53,400
Give them to me. All accounting documents

270
00:20:53,480 --> 00:20:56,360
are under my supervision.
I'll handle them myself.

271
00:20:58,600 --> 00:21:01,480
This is because of you, isn't it?
You put Father up to this investigation.

272
00:21:01,560 --> 00:21:03,400
Are you trying to frame me?

273
00:21:03,480 --> 00:21:06,360
I had nothing to do with it.
I don't know anything about this.

274
00:21:07,280 --> 00:21:09,560
Hathaya, don't play innocent
and act like the heroine.

275
00:21:10,200 --> 00:21:14,520
I see right through you. You claimed
you needed money for Grandma's treatment,

276
00:21:14,600 --> 00:21:16,840
but that was all a lie.

277
00:21:17,560 --> 00:21:19,960
You deliberately turned Grandpa against us

278
00:21:20,480 --> 00:21:22,280
because you want to take the inheritance.

279
00:21:22,960 --> 00:21:24,200
This has nothing to do with her.

280
00:21:26,440 --> 00:21:28,240
Take the documents to my office.

281
00:21:29,040 --> 00:21:29,920
Yes, sir.

282
00:21:32,320 --> 00:21:35,400
Mom, what are we going to do?

283
00:21:37,240 --> 00:21:38,920
I'll handle it myself.

284
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:44,280
Don't you have better things to do?
Mind your own business.

285
00:21:44,360 --> 00:21:45,800
Go do your job.

286
00:22:05,320 --> 00:22:08,680
Aunt Ann, is something wrong at home?

287
00:22:08,760 --> 00:22:11,040
Yes. Something serious.

288
00:22:11,120 --> 00:22:14,560
Miss Chayanee lied to Mr. Pichai.

289
00:22:15,160 --> 00:22:17,800
She told him she needed money
for an investment.

290
00:22:17,880 --> 00:22:19,720
But in reality,

291
00:22:19,800 --> 00:22:22,280
she gave the money to Raiwin

292
00:22:22,360 --> 00:22:25,040
for his election campaign. Now,

293
00:22:25,120 --> 00:22:29,480
he is furious and no longer
trusts Miss Chayanee or Ms. Liu.

294
00:22:31,520 --> 00:22:33,920
Okay. Thank you, Aunt Ann.

295
00:22:40,560 --> 00:22:43,280
Father, there are so many documents.

296
00:22:43,360 --> 00:22:45,400
Let me summarize them for you.

297
00:22:45,480 --> 00:22:48,120
No need. I can do it myself.

298
00:22:51,320 --> 00:22:53,480
You don't trust me anymore?

299
00:22:54,200 --> 00:22:55,200
That's right.

300
00:22:57,920 --> 00:22:59,080
I already told you.

301
00:22:59,760 --> 00:23:01,800
You used up all the trust I had in you.

302
00:23:01,880 --> 00:23:05,840
Father! I'm not okay
with you treating me like this.

303
00:23:05,920 --> 00:23:08,280
Why? What exactly are you not okay with?

304
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:11,800
I'm your daughter-in-law,

305
00:23:11,880 --> 00:23:13,280
but you're investigating me

306
00:23:13,360 --> 00:23:16,040
as if I were an outsider or an employee.

307
00:23:16,120 --> 00:23:19,320
How is anyone supposed
to respect me after this?

308
00:23:19,400 --> 00:23:22,800
Respect doesn't come
from being related to someone.

309
00:23:24,080 --> 00:23:26,400
It comes from your character
and your work.

310
00:23:29,160 --> 00:23:33,120
I'm trying to show every employee here

311
00:23:33,200 --> 00:23:34,720
that I run this business fairly.

312
00:23:36,600 --> 00:23:39,720
You're my daughter-in-law,
and you're my granddaughter.

313
00:23:39,800 --> 00:23:41,720
That relationship hasn't changed.

314
00:23:42,400 --> 00:23:45,160
But at work,
everyone has to be treated equally.

315
00:23:48,360 --> 00:23:49,960
You've always insisted

316
00:23:50,560 --> 00:23:53,640
that you work honestly.

317
00:23:55,000 --> 00:23:58,120
So instead of wasting your time
trying to explain yourself to me,

318
00:23:58,200 --> 00:24:00,600
let these documents give me the answer.

319
00:24:03,680 --> 00:24:05,720
If you have work to do, go do it.

320
00:24:06,400 --> 00:24:07,640
Yes, Grandpa.

321
00:24:14,200 --> 00:24:17,520
If Father checks
the purchase prices, he'll realize

322
00:24:17,600 --> 00:24:20,320
the numbers are higher than market prices.

323
00:24:20,840 --> 00:24:22,200
Don't panic yet, Mom.

324
00:24:22,280 --> 00:24:25,160
There are so many documents.
Grandpa can't possibly check all of them.

325
00:24:25,240 --> 00:24:27,000
What are we going to do now?

326
00:24:27,600 --> 00:24:30,480
I have to find a way
to get those documents out.

327
00:24:32,240 --> 00:24:33,760
All right, everyone.

328
00:24:34,320 --> 00:24:36,640
Go get lunch. Be back at one.

329
00:24:36,720 --> 00:24:38,440
Go. Go.

330
00:24:38,520 --> 00:24:39,760
Go.

331
00:24:40,840 --> 00:24:42,040
Go. Go.

332
00:24:44,560 --> 00:24:45,760
-Make it quick.
-Boss!

333
00:24:46,600 --> 00:24:49,440
You and Miss Hathaya both came to work.
Who's taking care of Papang?

334
00:24:49,520 --> 00:24:52,280
I asked Phon, the maid
from the main house, to help.

335
00:24:54,360 --> 00:24:55,960
Go. Go have lunch.

336
00:24:56,040 --> 00:24:58,840
-No. I've lost my appetite.
-What's wrong with you?

337
00:24:58,920 --> 00:25:02,000
Boss, did you forget? It'll be the end
of the month in just a few days.

338
00:25:02,080 --> 00:25:03,760
Miss Hathaya will have to go home.

339
00:25:03,840 --> 00:25:07,760
Without Miss Hathaya, the workers
are going to lose their morale.

340
00:25:08,520 --> 00:25:11,360
You make her sound
like some kind of guardian spirit.

341
00:25:11,440 --> 00:25:13,120
Come on, boss.

342
00:25:13,200 --> 00:25:16,480
She practically is.

343
00:25:16,560 --> 00:25:20,720
Miss Hathaya is like an angel.
She keeps all our workers motivated.

344
00:25:20,800 --> 00:25:23,720
And you'll be lonely too
when she's gone, won't you?

345
00:25:24,400 --> 00:25:27,840
Enough! You're talking nonsense. Go eat.

346
00:25:28,600 --> 00:25:29,880
Then come back to work.

347
00:25:30,960 --> 00:25:34,960
We'll miss her for sure.

348
00:25:45,320 --> 00:25:47,160
Ramil, are you looking for someone?

349
00:25:52,000 --> 00:25:52,840
No.

350
00:25:54,720 --> 00:25:58,320
I thought you came to see Hathaya.
I was going to tell you where she went.

351
00:26:00,120 --> 00:26:01,440
Wait!

352
00:26:03,760 --> 00:26:04,840
Where is…

353
00:26:05,600 --> 00:26:07,000
Hathaya?

354
00:26:09,680 --> 00:26:10,760
Come in.

355
00:26:19,080 --> 00:26:20,240
What do you want?

356
00:26:20,920 --> 00:26:23,320
I'm sorry for disturbing you, Grandpa.

357
00:26:23,400 --> 00:26:27,480
Since I'm not home to care for you,
I made you some Chinese herbal soup.

358
00:26:27,560 --> 00:26:29,600
I want you to stay healthy.

359
00:26:31,240 --> 00:26:32,200
Put it there.

360
00:26:34,000 --> 00:26:34,840
Is that all?

361
00:26:36,320 --> 00:26:39,200
-Yes.
-Go back to work.

362
00:27:00,480 --> 00:27:02,960
I hope you get some rest too, Grandpa.

363
00:27:06,120 --> 00:27:07,800
I don't want you getting stressed.

364
00:27:08,560 --> 00:27:11,200
If there's anything you want me
to help with, just tell me.

365
00:27:39,640 --> 00:27:42,040
Mom, Grandpa went out for lunch.

366
00:27:42,120 --> 00:27:45,360
I told all the employees
to take their break.

367
00:27:45,440 --> 00:27:46,640
Hurry. Go in and get that file.

368
00:27:56,760 --> 00:27:58,400
Go back to the office.

369
00:27:59,240 --> 00:28:02,920
What color is the file
with the purchase prices you altered?

370
00:28:03,000 --> 00:28:05,480
Red. We need to get that file out.

371
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:11,240
Mom, is that red file on the desk the one?

372
00:28:13,760 --> 00:28:16,480
Every purchase record is in this file.

373
00:28:20,920 --> 00:28:22,280
Yes. This is it.

374
00:28:24,160 --> 00:28:25,960
Father!

375
00:28:27,560 --> 00:28:29,320
Why did you come back?

376
00:28:31,240 --> 00:28:35,240
I was going to get lunch,
then I saw the two of you enter my office.

377
00:28:36,080 --> 00:28:37,040
What are you doing?

378
00:28:39,200 --> 00:28:40,800
I asked why you came in here.

379
00:28:45,800 --> 00:28:48,560
Mom came in to help
organize your documents.

380
00:28:49,280 --> 00:28:52,520
Yes. That's right.
I came in to sort them into categories

381
00:28:52,600 --> 00:28:55,080
so it would be easier
for you to inspect them.

382
00:28:56,320 --> 00:28:58,040
Is there anything I can help you with?

383
00:28:58,120 --> 00:29:00,160
No. I already have someone helping me.

384
00:29:00,240 --> 00:29:01,640
Who?

385
00:29:07,480 --> 00:29:10,600
I'm having Hathaya
inspect all the documents.

386
00:29:13,560 --> 00:29:16,840
Father, Hathaya isn't an auditor.

387
00:29:16,920 --> 00:29:18,000
She can't do this.

388
00:29:18,080 --> 00:29:19,480
Why not?

389
00:29:20,280 --> 00:29:23,560
Hathaya studied business administration.
She knows accounting.

390
00:29:24,280 --> 00:29:26,920
But Hathaya probably
only studied the basics.

391
00:29:27,000 --> 00:29:30,920
If you want help, Grandpa,
I have friends who are very good at this.

392
00:29:31,000 --> 00:29:33,480
I just want to know whether the income

393
00:29:33,560 --> 00:29:37,320
and receipts match, and whether
the purchase invoices match market prices.

394
00:29:37,400 --> 00:29:38,880
Hathaya can handle that.

395
00:29:39,520 --> 00:29:42,000
-Father.
-Both of you, get out.

396
00:29:43,480 --> 00:29:44,520
Go!

397
00:30:06,280 --> 00:30:10,200
Why do you trust me enough
to let me do this?

398
00:30:10,280 --> 00:30:14,120
I don't trust you.
I just trust outsiders even less.

399
00:30:16,200 --> 00:30:19,960
At least you have my son's blood in you.

400
00:30:22,440 --> 00:30:26,320
I hope you'll protect me
and safeguard my interests.

401
00:30:27,280 --> 00:30:30,200
Yes. I'll do this honestly.

402
00:30:31,200 --> 00:30:33,760
You have one day.

403
00:30:33,840 --> 00:30:35,560
I want an answer tomorrow.

404
00:30:37,800 --> 00:30:41,400
If you can't do it, tell me.
I'll have someone else do it.

405
00:30:42,280 --> 00:30:44,720
I can do it. I can do it, Grandpa.

406
00:30:49,520 --> 00:30:50,720
Excuse me.

407
00:31:06,600 --> 00:31:07,840
Thank you.

408
00:31:07,920 --> 00:31:11,400
Can you really handle all this? You're
selling houses and checking accounts.

409
00:31:12,080 --> 00:31:13,080
I can do it.

410
00:31:13,680 --> 00:31:15,600
-Good luck.
-Thank you.

411
00:31:24,800 --> 00:31:28,160
I don't understand why Grandpa
would let Hathaya inspect the accounts.

412
00:31:28,240 --> 00:31:31,800
We can't let this happen.
If Hathaya checks the books

413
00:31:31,880 --> 00:31:34,840
and finds out I've been stealing money,
she'll use it against me.

414
00:31:34,920 --> 00:31:38,360
Then Grandpa won't let me
handle the accounts anymore.

415
00:31:39,040 --> 00:31:42,040
And the inheritance will end up
being divided with Hathaya.

416
00:31:44,440 --> 00:31:48,640
If we can't find that file,
then we'll have to destroy the evidence.

417
00:31:54,080 --> 00:31:56,760
Without Miss Hathaya around,
we have to buy food.

418
00:31:56,840 --> 00:31:58,800
I'd rather eat her cooking.

419
00:31:59,360 --> 00:32:01,000
-Then don't eat any.
-I know.

420
00:32:01,080 --> 00:32:03,160
-Of course I'm eating.
-No food for you.

421
00:32:03,240 --> 00:32:05,280
I'm eating.

422
00:32:05,360 --> 00:32:06,600
Ramil.

423
00:32:06,680 --> 00:32:08,200
Hello.

424
00:32:11,240 --> 00:32:12,360
Why are you here, Mom?

425
00:32:13,360 --> 00:32:16,680
You shouldn't come here. This house
belongs to the son you don't love.

426
00:32:17,360 --> 00:32:21,120
You should spend your time
taking care of your husband instead.

427
00:32:23,600 --> 00:32:25,520
Mr. Saksit wants to talk to you.

428
00:32:25,600 --> 00:32:27,760
Then please tell him

429
00:32:27,840 --> 00:32:30,440
that if he wants to talk to me,
he can come see me.

430
00:32:33,440 --> 00:32:34,600
Alright.

431
00:32:40,960 --> 00:32:45,040
Come on, boss. Your mom is going
to get blamed by Mr. Saksit for this.

432
00:32:46,120 --> 00:32:48,920
That's her problem. Not mine.

433
00:32:52,040 --> 00:32:53,880
Daddy's home!

434
00:32:53,960 --> 00:32:56,600
Hey, Papang.

435
00:32:57,840 --> 00:32:59,520
-Miss me?
-I missed you, Daddy.

436
00:32:59,600 --> 00:33:02,320
I missed you too.

437
00:33:02,400 --> 00:33:06,520
Daddy and Uncle Max bought
lots of snacks and food. Let's go eat.

438
00:33:09,560 --> 00:33:12,320
What kind of mother are you?
You can't even control your own son.

439
00:33:13,520 --> 00:33:15,840
You let him become arrogant
enough to defy me

440
00:33:15,920 --> 00:33:18,160
while living in my house!

441
00:33:18,680 --> 00:33:20,760
I'm truly sorry on Ramil's behalf.

442
00:33:20,840 --> 00:33:23,480
I'm sure he didn't mean to refuse you.

443
00:33:23,560 --> 00:33:27,040
He's just exhausted from work,
and he also has to take care of Papang.

444
00:33:27,120 --> 00:33:30,080
That child is exactly why
I need to talk to him.

445
00:33:30,920 --> 00:33:34,200
Dad, I'll bring Ramil
to see you tomorrow morning.

446
00:33:34,280 --> 00:33:36,960
No. I'll go see him myself.

447
00:33:37,560 --> 00:33:39,120
He wants to challenge me?

448
00:33:40,600 --> 00:33:42,000
I'll go see him right now!

449
00:33:47,320 --> 00:33:48,200
Well?

450
00:33:48,280 --> 00:33:50,280
-Is it good?
-Yes.

451
00:33:50,360 --> 00:33:52,600
It's delicious, Daddy.

452
00:33:53,240 --> 00:33:54,120
Daddy.

453
00:33:54,200 --> 00:33:55,600
-Uncle Max.
-Yes?

454
00:33:55,680 --> 00:33:57,840
Do you know what pizza tastes best with?

455
00:33:57,920 --> 00:34:01,360
Ketchup.

456
00:34:01,440 --> 00:34:03,360
Wrong.

457
00:34:04,080 --> 00:34:05,840
Daddy, your turn.

458
00:34:07,320 --> 00:34:10,800
If it's not ketchup, then it must be

459
00:34:10,880 --> 00:34:12,320
soda.

460
00:34:12,400 --> 00:34:14,320
Wrong.

461
00:34:14,400 --> 00:34:16,920
Then you have to tell us. Daddy gives up.

462
00:34:17,000 --> 00:34:20,239
Pizza tastes best
when I eat it with Daddy.

463
00:34:20,320 --> 00:34:22,800
That's the cutest answer ever.

464
00:34:22,880 --> 00:34:25,560
How could Daddy not love you?

465
00:34:25,639 --> 00:34:26,960
So loved.

466
00:34:31,440 --> 00:34:32,520
-Here's some water.
-Thanks.

467
00:34:35,920 --> 00:34:38,960
Phon, thank you so much
for helping take care of Papang,

468
00:34:39,040 --> 00:34:43,280
but I think you should go back and rest.
Otherwise, they'll yell at you over there.

469
00:34:43,360 --> 00:34:44,239
Okay.

470
00:34:45,920 --> 00:34:49,120
-Come on. Let's eat.
-Where are the toppings?

471
00:34:51,800 --> 00:34:54,040
Hey! Who told you to come here?!

472
00:34:56,239 --> 00:34:59,240
I asked Phon to come
help take care of Papang.

473
00:35:04,040 --> 00:35:06,480
-Hello, Grandma.
-Hello, sweetheart.

474
00:35:09,360 --> 00:35:10,240
Hello, Grandpa.

475
00:35:12,200 --> 00:35:13,560
Get your filthy hands off me.

476
00:35:14,200 --> 00:35:16,400
I'm not your grandfather!

477
00:35:16,480 --> 00:35:18,920
Max. Take Papang to get cleaned up.

478
00:35:19,000 --> 00:35:20,080
Sure, boss.

479
00:35:20,160 --> 00:35:21,800
Come on.

480
00:35:24,040 --> 00:35:26,960
How could you say that to a child?
He knows nothing about any of this.

481
00:35:27,040 --> 00:35:30,320
Oh, really?
I was just teaching him manners.

482
00:35:31,280 --> 00:35:36,000
He shouldn't put
his dirty hands on other people.

483
00:35:36,880 --> 00:35:40,880
And more importantly,
I'm not his grandfather.

484
00:35:40,960 --> 00:35:44,200
You deny it even though
you know the truth perfectly well.

485
00:35:44,280 --> 00:35:45,640
Stop talking.

486
00:35:45,720 --> 00:35:49,000
I've told you many times
not to bring that child here.

487
00:35:49,080 --> 00:35:51,240
I did everything you told me.

488
00:35:51,320 --> 00:35:53,320
I let him stay with his mother

489
00:35:53,400 --> 00:35:56,880
and I rarely saw him.
He hardly knew who I was.

490
00:35:58,800 --> 00:36:00,400
But this time there was no choice.

491
00:36:01,080 --> 00:36:03,760
Nuchwara went out of town
and asked me to look after him.

492
00:36:03,840 --> 00:36:05,560
She'll be back to pick him up
in a few days.

493
00:36:06,520 --> 00:36:10,000
Really? If his mother
can't take care of him,

494
00:36:10,520 --> 00:36:12,280
leave him with someone else.

495
00:36:12,880 --> 00:36:16,000
You need to understand
the difference between a child and a pet.

496
00:36:16,080 --> 00:36:19,320
You can leave a pet
with someone else for a while.

497
00:36:19,400 --> 00:36:22,000
But a child needs care and attention.

498
00:36:22,880 --> 00:36:25,160
And the people best suited
to give a child that care

499
00:36:26,200 --> 00:36:30,280
are his parents and relatives.

500
00:36:30,360 --> 00:36:32,120
And most importantly,

501
00:36:32,800 --> 00:36:35,280
that child is your own blood.

502
00:36:35,360 --> 00:36:36,560
Enough.

503
00:36:37,160 --> 00:36:39,960
I didn't come here to waste time
talking about that kid.

504
00:36:40,040 --> 00:36:41,080
I came to warn you.

505
00:36:41,160 --> 00:36:45,120
You need to understand that Raiwin

506
00:36:45,200 --> 00:36:46,680
is about to run for office.

507
00:36:46,760 --> 00:36:48,720
And someone like you

508
00:36:48,800 --> 00:36:52,240
is not allowed to cause trouble for him.
Understand?

509
00:36:53,000 --> 00:36:53,880
Got it?

510
00:37:02,880 --> 00:37:05,920
Your master is gone.
Go follow him and serve him.

511
00:37:09,320 --> 00:37:10,560
Papang likes coconut jelly.

512
00:37:11,400 --> 00:37:14,360
I made some for him. Give it to him later.

513
00:37:18,960 --> 00:37:20,800
Unless it's necessary,

514
00:37:23,240 --> 00:37:24,720
don't come to this house again.

515
00:37:27,800 --> 00:37:28,880
You can go.

516
00:37:51,760 --> 00:37:54,160
Hathaya, are you heading home?
I can give you a ride.

517
00:37:54,240 --> 00:37:57,680
I'm not finished yet, Ploy.
You should go ahead.

518
00:37:57,760 --> 00:37:59,640
-Okay. See you.
-Drive safely.

519
00:37:59,720 --> 00:38:01,120
-Bye.
-Bye.

520
00:38:07,240 --> 00:38:09,000
Your precious little boy finally asleep?

521
00:38:09,080 --> 00:38:12,160
It took forever. He played games

522
00:38:12,240 --> 00:38:13,440
until the phone died.

523
00:38:13,520 --> 00:38:15,720
Boss.

524
00:38:15,800 --> 00:38:17,880
When did you buy this coconut jelly?
It's amazing.

525
00:38:19,760 --> 00:38:21,440
Just eat. Stop asking so many questions.

526
00:38:22,040 --> 00:38:24,000
Want some?

527
00:38:24,080 --> 00:38:26,240
No. You eat it.

528
00:38:27,920 --> 00:38:29,640
HATHAYA: MAX, I'M STAYING
AT THE OFFICE TONIGHT

529
00:38:29,720 --> 00:38:32,280
Miss Hathaya says she's sleeping
at the office tonight.

530
00:38:34,600 --> 00:38:35,920
She didn't message me.

531
00:38:37,480 --> 00:38:40,000
Well, you're mean as hell.
Who would want to talk to you?

532
00:38:40,080 --> 00:38:43,840
She's sleeping at the office?
Where is she even going to sleep?

533
00:38:43,920 --> 00:38:48,280
Why? Oh, you're worried about her.

534
00:38:48,360 --> 00:38:50,960
Do you have feelings for her or something?

535
00:38:51,040 --> 00:38:52,160
No.

536
00:38:53,320 --> 00:38:55,800
-You never worry about me.
-Why would I? You're a grown man.

537
00:38:55,880 --> 00:38:56,920
Wow. This is good.

538
00:39:19,360 --> 00:39:21,440
-Excuse me.
-Yes?

539
00:39:21,960 --> 00:39:24,240
Is the food stall at the front still open?

540
00:39:24,320 --> 00:39:28,080
That place stays open late. If you want
something, I can go buy it for you.

541
00:39:28,160 --> 00:39:30,360
That's okay. I'll go eat there.

542
00:39:30,440 --> 00:39:32,880
Could I borrow your bicycle?

543
00:39:32,960 --> 00:39:34,160
Of course.

544
00:39:34,680 --> 00:39:36,960
Thank you so much.

545
00:39:38,080 --> 00:39:40,880
I'll go finish checking
the inside of the development.

546
00:39:40,960 --> 00:39:43,840
Then when I'm done with the bike,
I'll leave it at the security booth.

547
00:39:43,920 --> 00:39:46,200
-Sure.
-Okay. Thank you.

548
00:39:58,920 --> 00:40:00,160
Hathaya is gone.

549
00:40:00,240 --> 00:40:04,040
That accounting file
has to be on her desk.

550
00:40:04,120 --> 00:40:06,120
I brought the spare key card.

551
00:40:06,200 --> 00:40:08,880
Keep watch, Mom. I'll handle it.

552
00:40:09,680 --> 00:40:12,200
Make sure you get that file.

553
00:40:12,280 --> 00:40:15,680
Without it, Grandpa can't prove
anything against me.

554
00:40:15,760 --> 00:40:16,760
Okay, Mom.

555
00:40:35,040 --> 00:40:36,120
My wallet!

556
00:40:45,840 --> 00:40:47,600
Oh my God! Hathaya!

557
00:40:47,680 --> 00:40:48,880
BUDGET ACCOUNT

558
00:40:51,120 --> 00:40:52,000
Chayanee!

559
00:40:53,080 --> 00:40:55,480
Why did you come in?
You're supposed to be keeping watch.

560
00:40:55,560 --> 00:40:57,320
Hathaya is back.

561
00:40:57,920 --> 00:40:59,280
Hurry!

562
00:41:02,080 --> 00:41:03,640
Then we have to destroy everything.

563
00:41:03,720 --> 00:41:05,200
2018 BUDGET SUMMARY

564
00:41:12,600 --> 00:41:13,840
REVENUE AND EXPENSES

565
00:41:15,040 --> 00:41:17,080
Hurry!

566
00:41:17,160 --> 00:41:18,560
Let's go!

567
00:41:27,160 --> 00:41:28,200
What's that smell?

568
00:41:30,840 --> 00:41:32,120
Fire.

569
00:41:40,080 --> 00:41:41,440
Hathaya, move!

570
00:41:51,520 --> 00:41:54,400
I can't finish checking
the accounts for Grandpa now.

571
00:41:54,480 --> 00:41:55,920
All the documents burned.

572
00:41:57,440 --> 00:41:58,760
How did the fire start?

573
00:42:09,880 --> 00:42:11,160
A fuel can.

574
00:42:12,440 --> 00:42:14,120
Someone deliberately
burned these documents.

575
00:42:15,680 --> 00:42:16,680
Who do you think did it?

576
00:42:17,800 --> 00:42:19,080
I don't know.

577
00:42:31,160 --> 00:42:33,600
Ramil had to stick
his nose into this again.

578
00:42:34,280 --> 00:42:38,200
Forget about him, Mom.
We destroyed all the evidence anyway.

579
00:42:39,560 --> 00:42:41,880
If Hathaya can't give Grandpa an answer,

580
00:42:41,960 --> 00:42:44,760
I'd like to see what he says.

581
00:42:52,040 --> 00:42:55,960
I found a fuel can. Someone deliberately
set the documents on fire.

582
00:42:57,040 --> 00:42:59,000
Did you check the security cameras?

583
00:42:59,080 --> 00:43:03,280
They're still wiring that area.
The cameras haven't been installed yet.

584
00:43:05,760 --> 00:43:07,480
Did anyone enter or leave the development?

585
00:43:10,520 --> 00:43:14,080
Well? Did anyone
come in or out that night?

586
00:43:15,920 --> 00:43:19,000
If you don't want to lose your job,
keep your mouth shut.

587
00:43:20,040 --> 00:43:20,960
No, sir.

588
00:43:25,720 --> 00:43:27,320
Go. Get back to work.

589
00:43:28,040 --> 00:43:29,160
Yes, sir.

590
00:43:33,680 --> 00:43:35,520
I'll ask the police to help investigate.

591
00:43:36,880 --> 00:43:38,920
-No.
-Why, sir?

592
00:43:39,000 --> 00:43:41,280
I don't want bad news getting out.

593
00:43:41,920 --> 00:43:45,880
It could affect existing buyers
and new customers.

594
00:43:47,320 --> 00:43:48,200
Yes, sir.

595
00:43:53,880 --> 00:43:54,920
Grandpa.

596
00:43:55,920 --> 00:43:58,720
I'm sorry the important documents
were burned.

597
00:44:00,800 --> 00:44:04,200
Father, this is a very serious matter.

598
00:44:04,280 --> 00:44:07,920
Those were all the company's
accounting records.

599
00:44:08,600 --> 00:44:12,000
I warned you not to let
Hathaya handle this.

600
00:44:14,560 --> 00:44:16,240
Mom.

601
00:44:18,040 --> 00:44:20,400
Don't make Hathaya feel worse.

602
00:44:21,360 --> 00:44:23,680
She must already be devastated.

603
00:44:23,760 --> 00:44:27,800
Look. She even packed up
all her things and came to resign.

604
00:44:35,080 --> 00:44:36,280
You came to resign?

605
00:44:37,880 --> 00:44:38,920
No.

606
00:44:39,800 --> 00:44:42,840
I'm sorry that some
of the documents were burned,

607
00:44:42,920 --> 00:44:46,560
but all the important
procurement records are still intact.

608
00:44:52,720 --> 00:44:55,520
I finished checking
these documents yesterday.

609
00:44:59,840 --> 00:45:01,600
2022 BUDGET SUMMARY

610
00:45:04,000 --> 00:45:06,000
The documents that burned

611
00:45:06,080 --> 00:45:08,880
were utility bills and other expenses.

612
00:45:08,960 --> 00:45:12,080
I checked with Accounting. They still
have those records saved in the system.

613
00:45:12,160 --> 00:45:14,880
And what about what I asked you to check?

614
00:45:19,480 --> 00:45:23,040
Well? Did you find any discrepancies?

615
00:45:23,120 --> 00:45:24,640
Aunt Liu's…

616
00:45:26,320 --> 00:45:27,840
accounting…

617
00:45:30,880 --> 00:45:32,120
is correct.

618
00:45:33,440 --> 00:45:35,760
None of the expenses were inflated.

619
00:45:45,240 --> 00:45:46,400
Thank you.

620
00:45:47,720 --> 00:45:51,000
You're welcome. I'll get back to work now.

621
00:45:58,040 --> 00:45:59,760
-Liu.
-Yes.

622
00:46:00,720 --> 00:46:03,360
Take the documents back
and return to work.

623
00:46:03,440 --> 00:46:04,560
Yes.

624
00:46:19,320 --> 00:46:20,320
Ramil.

625
00:46:21,160 --> 00:46:23,880
I want to discuss
installing security cameras

626
00:46:24,560 --> 00:46:26,560
and expanding Phase Two.

627
00:46:27,560 --> 00:46:28,400
Yes, sir.

628
00:46:31,600 --> 00:46:32,680
How is it?

629
00:46:33,760 --> 00:46:35,160
Okay.

630
00:46:38,520 --> 00:46:40,880
You. Leave us.

631
00:46:41,480 --> 00:46:43,520
I need to speak privately with Hathaya.

632
00:46:50,240 --> 00:46:53,600
Aunt Liu, Chaya,
what do you want to talk about?

633
00:46:53,680 --> 00:46:56,240
I have to go take care of customers.

634
00:46:56,320 --> 00:46:58,280
Don't act hardworking just to look good.

635
00:47:00,040 --> 00:47:03,520
And stop pretending
to be such a good person.

636
00:47:06,560 --> 00:47:07,880
What do you want?

637
00:47:11,440 --> 00:47:13,320
What are you talking about, Aunt Liu?

638
00:47:14,400 --> 00:47:17,280
You checked those accounts.

639
00:47:18,080 --> 00:47:19,680
You know money is missing.

640
00:47:23,200 --> 00:47:26,040
Why didn't you tell Grandpa the truth

641
00:47:26,120 --> 00:47:27,600
that Mom embezzled money?

642
00:47:33,840 --> 00:47:37,640
I know about Chaya giving money to Raiwin.

643
00:47:38,800 --> 00:47:42,240
I just don't want Grandpa to be hurt
and disappointed more than he already is.

644
00:47:42,320 --> 00:47:44,000
I'm worried about his feelings.

645
00:47:44,720 --> 00:47:47,600
Don't give me that crap
about caring about Grandpa's health.

646
00:47:47,680 --> 00:47:50,000
You're just putting on a show
to make yourself look good.

647
00:47:53,480 --> 00:47:56,160
If I had told Grandpa the whole truth,

648
00:47:56,240 --> 00:47:58,520
that would be putting on a show.

649
00:47:58,600 --> 00:48:00,360
Like I was trying to get the inheritance,

650
00:48:00,920 --> 00:48:03,280
just like you accused me of before.

651
00:48:05,520 --> 00:48:07,200
Then why help us?

652
00:48:08,400 --> 00:48:10,080
I already told you.

653
00:48:10,880 --> 00:48:12,480
I feel guilty

654
00:48:12,560 --> 00:48:16,240
because I played a part
in your father's death.

655
00:48:17,320 --> 00:48:19,840
I hope what I'm doing

656
00:48:19,920 --> 00:48:22,080
can make up for some of that.

657
00:48:22,960 --> 00:48:24,200
I want us to be a family.

658
00:48:29,600 --> 00:48:32,320
I'm asking you.
Please don't do anything wrong again.

659
00:48:37,720 --> 00:48:39,680
I'm worried about Grandpa's feelings

660
00:48:40,200 --> 00:48:42,160
and his health.

661
00:48:42,800 --> 00:48:44,560
I need to get back to work.

662
00:48:55,560 --> 00:48:57,000
What should we do?

663
00:48:57,840 --> 00:48:59,880
Should we do what she asked?

664
00:49:01,000 --> 00:49:03,440
She thinks doing good
can erase what she did.

665
00:49:03,520 --> 00:49:05,640
I will never forgive her.

666
00:49:05,720 --> 00:49:08,120
Don't do anything for now.

667
00:49:08,200 --> 00:49:10,680
She only has a few days left
before she has to go home.

668
00:49:12,720 --> 00:49:16,160
Once she leaves,
everything will go back to normal.

669
00:49:17,720 --> 00:49:20,800
Everything Grandpa owns
has to belong to me.

670
00:49:21,680 --> 00:49:24,680
Grandpa can only have
one favorite granddaughter.

671
00:49:33,200 --> 00:49:36,400
May I go upstairs and pay
my respects to Dad's ashes?

672
00:49:36,480 --> 00:49:39,360
You should go home.

673
00:49:39,920 --> 00:49:42,040
Your family has probably been
waiting for you for a long time.

674
00:49:42,120 --> 00:49:43,280
NEXT EPISODE

675
00:49:43,360 --> 00:49:45,840
Your husband took off
his clothes and tried to rape me,

676
00:49:45,920 --> 00:49:47,600
and you still think it's no big deal?

677
00:49:47,680 --> 00:49:49,800
He didn't actually do anything to you.

678
00:49:49,880 --> 00:49:52,720
Everyone there branded me
as being just like you.

679
00:49:53,240 --> 00:49:55,240
We'll start a new life.

680
00:49:55,320 --> 00:49:57,280
We won't be parasites
living off anyone anymore.

681
00:50:00,880 --> 00:50:02,480
Grandma!

682
00:51:56,760 --> 00:51:58,760
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen
